            <ArticleTitle>Ingested magnets: the force within.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>466-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Foreign body ingestion is a common occurrence in children. Morbidity associated with ingestion is rare and is dependent on the type of foreign body ingested. We report a case of a 9-year-old boy who developed intestinal obstruction and perforation following ingestion of magnetic-backed earrings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
